This repository is a TEST FIXTURE. Its intent graphs deliberately carry, in the
fields an application displays, characters that close an HTML element, open one,
or name a URL scheme a browser executes. They exist so that a test can prove an
application shows repository content as characters rather than acting on it.

Nothing here attacks anybody or anything. The payloads set one sentinel —
`document.documentElement.dataset.smokePwned` — on the document that executed
them, and do nothing else: no network request, no storage, no navigation. The
sentinel exists so a test can tell "the browser executed this" apart from "the
browser displayed the words of it", a distinction that searching for the
payload's own text cannot make.

Do not compose these graphs into a real project. They are inputs to a test, not
guidance for anything.
